  "title": "Town of Florida, MA — Official Website",
  "text": "Town of Florida, MA — Official Website\nSkip to main content\nFlorida\nMassachusetts\nHome\nHistory\nOfficials\nAgendas, Minutes & Reports\nAnnouncements\nForms\nContact\nHome\nHistory\nTown Officials\nAgendas, Minutes & Reports\nTown Announcements\nForms & Documents\nContact Town Hall\nSearch\nTown of\nFlorida\n379 Mohawk Trail, Drury, MA 01343\nFlorida — the place to be Friends of the Forest\nOfficial Town Website\nScroll\nPay Taxes\nTown Officials\nContact Us\nAgendas, Minutes & Reports\nAnnouncements\nForms & Docs\nTown History\n379 Mohawk Trail, Drury, MA 01343\n(413) 662-2448 ext. 0\nM, T, Th, F: 8:30am–4:00pm · Wednesday: 12:00pm–7:30pm\nTownAdmin@TownOfFlorida.org\n🌲\nBerkshire County, Massachusetts\nWelcome to\nFlorida, MA\nFlorida is a town in Berkshire County, Massachusetts, United States. Part of the Pittsfield Metropolitan Statistical Area, it is home to the eastern portal of the Hoosac Tunnel and sits at an elevation of 2,172 feet — the highest point on the Mohawk Trail.\nIncorporated in 1805, Florida is governed by an open town meeting form of government, led by a Board of Selectmen and served by a dedicated team of departments and volunteers.\nRead Our History\nMeet Our Officials\n1805\nIncorporated\n2,172\nft\nPeak Elevation\n92%\nForest Cover\n4.75\nmi\nHoosac Tunnel\n🏛️\nTown Services\nDepartments & Services\nFind contact information and hours for every town department.\nElected Board\nBoard of Selectmen\nNeil Oleson (Chair) · Meets every other Wednesday at 6:00pm\n(413) 662-2448 ext. 0\nTown Clerk\nTown Clerk\nLisa H. Brown · Wednesday Evenings 6:00–7:30pm\nClerk@TownOfFlorida.org\nBoard\nBoard of Assessors\nKrista Bishop, Lawrence Cote, Susan Bedini\nMeets every other Monday at 6:00pm\nDepartment\nHighway Department\nJames White, Supervisor · Hours: 7:00am–3:30pm\nHighway@TownOfFlorida.org\nEmergency Services\nFlorida Volunteer Fire Dept.\nMichael Gleason, FVFD Chief · 139 Mohawk Trail\nBurn Permits: Tuesday Nights 6–9pm\nEmergency Services\nPolice Department\nMA State Police — Cheshire Barracks\nEmergencies: 911 · Non-emergency: (413) 743-4700\nView All Departments\n📢\nWhat's Happening\nTown Announcements\nLatest news, events, and notices from the Town of Florida.\nNorth Berkshire Vocational Agenda — October 8, 2026\nMeeting agenda posted October 8, 2026.\nZero Waste Day — Saturday, November 14\nFree regional recycling event hosted by NBSWMD, Saturday, November 14, 9:00 AM to 12:00 PM, at Community House, 191 Church Street, Cheshire, MA. Open to residents of participating towns, including Florida -- please bring proof of town residence.\nTrick-or-Treat — Saturday, October 31\nTrick-or-treat hours for the Town of Florida: Saturday, October 31, 5:00 to 7:30 pm. Please keep your outside lights on to welcome our children.\nHalloween Celebration at the Senior Center — October 30\nJoin us for a Halloween celebration at the Senior Center, Friday, October 30 from 6 to 7 pm. Bring the kids — candy and refreshments provided.\nWarrant for 2026 State Election — Tuesday, November 3\nOfficial warrant for the 2026 State Election. Polls open at the Town Office Building, 379 Mohawk Trail, Drury, MA, from 7:00 AM to 8:00 PM.\n2026 State & Federal Election Calendar\nEarly voting schedule and polling hours for the November 3, 2026 State & Federal Election. Last day to register to vote: October 24, 2026.\nTown Offices Closed — Columbus Day, Monday, October 12, 2026\nTown Hall, the Highway Department, and the Senior/Community Center will be closed in observance of Columbus Day.\n4th Annual Haunted Hayride — October 24\nFlorida Volunteer Fire Department's 4th Annual Haunted Hayride, October 24, opens at 6:30 p.m. Rides start at Chilson's Pond, 80 Tilda Hill Road, Florida, MA. $10 per person, children 5 and under free. Free hot cider, cocoa, and popcorn; adult and children Halloween basket raffles; hotdogs and Halloween baked goods for sale on site (cash and credit cards accepted). All proceeds benefit the Florida Volunteer Fire Dept.\nSchool Opens Wednesday, August 26 — Please Drive Safely\nSchool starts Wednesday, August 26, 2026. Please stop for school buses, slow down, eliminate distractions, watch for pedestrians and students, and give yourself extra time — help keep our children safe.\nNBESS Steering Committee Meeting — August 26, 2026\nNotice and agenda for the North Berkshire Educational Sustainability Study Steering Committee meeting, Wednesday, August 26 at 5:00 p.m. at Mount Greylock Regional High School (in-person or via Zoom).\nView All Announcements\nGet In Touch\nWe're Here to Help\nTown Hall is open Monday, Tuesday, Thursday & Friday 8:30am–4:00pm and Wednesday 12:00pm–7:30pm.\nContact Town Hall\n(413) 662-2448 ext. 0\nTown of Florida, Massachusetts\nFlorida — the place to be Friends of the Forest.\nIncorporated 1805. Berkshire County, MA.\nNavigation\nHome\nHistory\nTown Officials\nAgendas, Minutes & Reports\nAnnouncements\nForms\nContact\nDepartments\nBoard of Selectmen\nTown Clerk\nBoard of Assessors\nHighway Dept.\nFire Department\nFlorida Free Library\nContact\n379 Mohawk Trail, Drury, MA 01343\n(413) 662-2448\nTownAdmin@TownOfFlorida.org\n©\nTown of Florida, Massachusetts. All rights reserved.  ·\nAccessibility\n·\nPrivacy Policy\nPowered by\nBerkshire IT",
